// Lok Sabha constituency boundaries for IndiaMap (level: 'pc').
//
// SOURCE: datta07/INDIAN-SHAPEFILES, INDIA/INDIA_PARLIMENTARY_BOUNDARIES.json
// (MIT). 543 constituencies, 2008 delimitation. `code` is the PC number
// within its state. State is assigned by largest overlap with the DataMeet
// state layer (so Telangana's 17 and Ladakh's 1 come out right; counts per
// state match the official 543 exactly).
// CAVEAT: Assam was re-delimited in 2023; its 14 shapes here are the OLD
// boundaries. Don't publish an Assam constituency map from this file.
// One extra unit has name/code null: Gilgit-Baltistan and Aksai Chin, which
// no constituency covers. It is drawn as plain land so the outline is whole.
// Simplified with mapshaper (interval 2.5 km, keep-shapes), lon/lat to 3 dp.
//
// THE OUTLINE IS INDIA'S OFFICIAL ONE (Survey of India 2019 political map).
// Checked 2026-10-27 against DataMeet's Survey of India national outline: the
// northern boundary matches; differences are coastal slivers only (Gulf of
// Kutch, Mumbai harbour, Sundarbans). Never swap in Natural Earth / GADM / OSM.
// Rebuild: .claude/skills/india-map/build-geo.sh
//
// Shape: { u: [[name, state, code, [lon,lat] label point, rings], ...],
//          s: { State: rings } }  -- s is dissolved from u, so borders align.
